{"id":"chatcmpl-1787e781-2123-4f6d-a602-05dbfe689412","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246464,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model consensus strategy for medical image interpretation when a single model's output is unreliable. The key insight is that conflicting or incoherent outputs from independent models should trigger a verification step rather than majority voting. The final answer was validated by an explicit verifier despite initial disagreement, showing that structured conflict resolution outperforms naive aggregation.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When multiple independent models disagree on a visual finding, invoke an explicit verification/audit step rather than defaulting to majority vote or first response.\",\n    \"Query each model with the same anatomically-grounded question (specifying landmarks and laterality) to make outputs comparable and reduce ambiguity.\",\n    \"Detect and flag incoherent or non-responsive model outputs as low-confidence signals, and weight remaining coherent outputs more heavily.\",\n    \"Use a domain-expert tool first to establish an anatomical baseline, then cross-validate with general-purpose models to catch expert-tool blind spots.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Ask each model the same landmark-specific question (e.g., costophrenic angles, laterality) so answers are directly comparable; treat incoherent outputs as abstentions.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus\": \"Prefer structured conflict resolution (explicit verifier) over majority voting when model outputs conflict or when one model abstains.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual findings\": \"Anchor questions to concrete anatomical landmarks and require laterality specification to disambiguate left/right findings.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before finalizing, confirm whether any model output was incoherent or abstained, and whether a verifier was invoked to resolve conflicts.\",\n    \"Confirm the question posed to each model specified anatomical landmarks and laterality so outputs are directly comparable.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":656,"total_tokens":1030,"completion_tokens":374,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":656},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":374}}}